# Aston Martin DBS six-cylinder coupe, 1967-1972.
#
# William Towns's DBS on the shortened Lagonda chassis: the flat bonnet with the
# shallow raised central vent, the wide fine-mesh grille with four round
# headlamps, the flat rear deck and one rectangular rear lamp housing per side,
# divided into three lens sections. 787 six-cylinder cars built; the DBS V8 of
# 1970-72 is a different nose and is not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DBS
#
# Dimensions 4.580 x 1.830 x 1.330 m, wheelbase 2.610 m.
#
# Shape reference: three six-cylinder DBS coupes. Image 1 is a 1969 blue car in
# true near-level side elevation, only 664 x 302 px, so it governs the flank and
# roofline but not fine detail. Image 2 is a pale 1968 car, front three-quarter,
# and shows the four round lamps, the wide grille and the shallow raised central
# bonnet vent that is modelled here (not the DBS V8's large open scoop). Image 3
# is a red 1971 car, rear three-quarter, and shows the single segmented rear lamp
# housing per side.
#
# Colours: grade (c), the DBS register's production record of 793 identified
# cars. The four most common are Silver Birch (107), Dubonnet Rosso (80),
# Platinum (76) and Aquamarine (55); Pacific Blue (34) and Goodwood Green (14)
# are used here for visual range. Weights 4, 3, 2, 1, total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 240 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65: a longer, more
# spacious cabin than the DB6's, with the same low roofline. Classes 3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1967 intro, retires staggered 1985-1986 on an
# eighteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-dbs.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-dbs.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-dbs/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the quarter-window outline is more angular than the
# photograph's, and the rear lamp panel lacks the recessed surround. At 128 px
# the long bonnet, four-lamp grille, flat rear deck and segmented tail lamps
# read as a DBS.

obj=citycar
name=AstonDBS(SilverBirch)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=4
intro_year=1967
intro_month=10
retire_year=1986
retire_month=6
speed=240
length=3
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=428

Image[E]=./images/aston-dbs-silverbirch_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/aston-dbs-silverbirch_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/aston-dbs-silverbirch_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/aston-dbs-silverbirch_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/aston-dbs-silverbirch_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/aston-dbs-silverbirch_NW.0.0,12,10
Image[N]=./images/aston-dbs-silverbirch_N.0.0,0,33
